# What became of a message we sent: the three marks a bubble's corner can carry.
#
# One outbound message per state, in the order they happen - sent and waiting, acknowledged,
# refused - so the clock, the double tick and the alert circle are on one frame and can be told
# apart at a glance rather than described. The last one carries a reason, which is the other
# half of the change: a reason is a sentence, so it goes under the message as a supporting line
# instead of into the corner where it used to push the whole run outside the bubble.
#
# `ack` is its own verb because a Routing reply is the one thing about a message that arrives
# after it, and no press this harness can make produces one - `message out` leaves a bubble
# pending, which is one of the three and the only one a scene could otherwise reach.
scene demo
scale 4
clock 2026-01-12 19:12
config

message out ALFA Heading for the saddle now
ack sending
hold 600

message out ALFA Should be there before dark
ack delivered
hold 600

# Routing_Error 35 is PKI_UNKNOWN_PUBKEY: the longest reason the catalog carries, and the one
# that used to be wider than the bubble it was drawn in.
message out ALFA Bring the spare antenna
ack failed 35
hold 900

# The cursor over each of them: a selected bubble is a different fill with an accent bar laid
# outside it, and the marks have to stay legible against both.
key a
hold 400
key up 2
hold 700
